  "body": "## What happens\n\nThe Recipes tab (U11, #4337) shows the feed in mm/min for each material row, and a derived line under the row shows the chip load (feed per tooth, fz) and the surface speed (Vc). The user can type only the feed in mm/min. Many machinists think in feed per tooth and surface speed.\n\n## Requested\n\nThe user asked in chat on 2026-11-27: \"Would it be an idea if we could switch between feed per tooth and feed mm/min? Or adjust one automatically when we edit the other?\"\n\n## Proposal\n\n- Each recipe row can show and edit the feed as fz (mm per tooth) or as F (mm/min). A switch in the tab header selects the mode, or the row shows both fields.\n- When the user edits one value, the other value follows: F = fz × flutes × rpm. In the same way, the spindle speed and Vc follow each other: rpm = Vc × 1000 / (π × D).\n- The stored value stays the same as today (one source of truth), so the project file does not change. The other value is derived.\n- An edit is one undoable command, as today.\n- A tool with no flute count, or a zero diameter, refuses the fz or Vc input with a reason. It never divides by zero.\n\n## Done means\n\n- Tests: an fz edit sets F, an F edit sets fz, an rpm edit and a Vc edit follow each other, and each edit is one undo step. The refusal for a missing flute count or a zero diameter has a test.\n- Before and after screenshots in the PR.\n",
